    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you find yourself doing anything specific to try to hide or fix this asymmetry, such as constantly checking mirrors, avoiding certain angles, or using your hair or clothing to cover that side of your face?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S068",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, I do a lot of that. Um, especially before I leave for school. I usually get stuck in the bathroom just... checking my face in the mirror over and over. And then I'll use my phone camera to see how it looks from different angles. \n\nI try to fix my hair to cover it up, or I'll keep changing my shirt to see if a different collar makes my jaw look less crooked. I also end up asking my mom if it looks weird, just... hoping she'll tell me something that makes me feel better, even though I know I won't really believe her. \n\nSometimes I get so caught up doing all of this that I actually miss my lab entirely. Or if I do make it, I'm just so drained from the whole morning that I can't even focus on my programming work.",
